{"id":"doc:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-14-mulesoft-munit-hardening.md#task-6-add-local-sample-project-acceptance-checking","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-14-mulesoft-munit-hardening.md","heading":"Task 6: Add local sample-project acceptance checking","level":3,"anchor":"task-6-add-local-sample-project-acceptance-checking","span":{"start":215,"end":256},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:b16371b6cfb6fa3000da2f20d784bea6b27cf95a760f64aca2fa395267d89516","meta":{"codeRefs":["scripts/check-mule-sample.mjs","scripts/fixtures/synthetic-mule-project.mjs","package.json","scripts/check-mule-sample.test.mjs","syntheticMuleProject(root)","js\nconst expected = {\n  flows: 18, subflows: 7, flowRefs: 39, choices: 10, transforms: 27,\n  inlineDw2: 30, listeners: 2, apiOperations: 8, outboundCalls: 4,\n  errorHandlers: 15, productionDwl: 1, testDwl: 21, munitTests: 6,\n  mocks: 6, externalFlowTargets: 3,\n};","Require","and reject missing/non-file inputs. Run the built CLI into a temporary registry/cache, read graph JSONL through public soul APIs, calculate counts, assert zero raw property values and zero symbols from",", print a table, and exit nonzero on a mismatch. Never copy or stage the archive.\n\nImplement","as a deterministic fixture generator: create 18 flows, 7 subflows, 39 flow refs (three unique unresolved targets), 10 choices, 27 transforms, 30 inline DW2 blocks, 2 listeners, 8 APIKit operations, 4 outbound HTTP requests, 15 error handlers, one production",", 21 test","files, and 6 MUnit tests with one mock each. Include ordinary and secure property canaries plus generated report JavaScript so the same fixture verifies extraction altitude and redaction.\n\nAdd root script:",".\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Verify against the supplied sample locally**\n\nRun:","Expected: all approved acceptance counts PASS, secrets found = 0, report-JS symbols = 0.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Commit only the checker**","bash\ngit add scripts/check-mule-sample.mjs scripts/check-mule-sample.test.mjs package.json\ngit commit -m \"test: add local Mule sample acceptance gate\"","const","expected","flows","18","subflows","flowRefs","39","choices","10","transforms","27","inlineDw2","30","listeners","apiOperations","outboundCalls","errorHandlers","15","productionDwl","testDwl","21","munitTests","mocks","externalFlowTargets","git","add","scripts/check","mule","sample.mjs","sample.test.mjs","commit","test","local","Mule","sample","acceptance","gate"],"links":[]}}
{"id":"doc:docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-14-mulesoft-munit-hardening.md#task-7-document-support-and-expose-concise-diagnostics","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-14-mulesoft-munit-hardening.md","heading":"Task 7: Document support and expose concise diagnostics","level":3,"anchor":"task-7-document-support-and-expose-concise-diagnostics","span":{"start":257,"end":303},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:8e28e545a8491bbcd7940b7dfcec0e3e3657395fa10b4e2411833319266aa4bf","meta":{"codeRefs":["docs/mulesoft.md","README.md","packages/cli/src/cli.ts","packages/cli/src/cli.test.ts","--json","mulesoft","ts\ninterface MuleIndexSummary {\n  projects: number;\n  dialectFiles: { mule3: number; mule4: number };\n  flows: number;\n  subflows: number;\n  routes: number;\n  flowRefs: number;\n  transforms: number;\n  munitTests: number;\n  externalTargets: number;\n  references: { resolved: number; unresolved: number };\n  diagnostics: { warnings: number; errors: number };\n}","Derive counts from classified files, emitted nodes/edges, and parse diagnostics. Do not make index success depend on warning count; error diagnostics for individual files are reported while the rest of the project remains queryable.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Write user documentation**\n\nDocument directory/ZIP/JAR examples, archive cache location,",", Mule 3/4 detection, supported constructs, property key-only behavior, denied secure resources, MUnit semantics, unresolved placeholders, archive-update behavior, unsupported watch/Git ownership for archives, and the non-goal of Java generation.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Verify docs and CLI tests, then commit**\n\nRun:","Expected: PASS.","bash\ngit add docs/mulesoft.md README.md packages/cli/src/cli.ts packages/cli/src/cli.test.ts\ngit commit -m \"docs: document MuleSoft extraction\"","interface","MuleIndexSummary","projects","number","dialectFiles","mule3","mule4","flows","subflows","routes","flowRefs","transforms","munitTests","externalTargets","referen